title: 'Technical : Relationships between atoms can have authors.'
pid: 87d78e2f-73e4-4047-92a2-f53c81bccac2
body: |2-
  This might have advantages for granular privacy.
  Skg permits it, but by default I think it is more natural that
  relationships be defined by one of the atoms involved,
  usually the left member:
  - the container,
  - link source
  - the subscriber
  - the overrider
  - the subscriber connected (via a subscribee) to a hidden node
